Select the runtime provider
Set agent.provider in .crosslink/hook-config.json, or in the gitignored .crosslink/hook-config.local.json for a per-machine choice:
{
  "agent": {
    "provider": "codex"
  }
}
Valid providers are "claude", "codex", and "custom". agent.binary is only an executable-path override; it does not change the selected protocol:
{
  "agent": {
    "provider": "codex",
    "binary": "/opt/wrappers/company-codex"
  }
}
custom requires agent.binary and supports interactive prompt-on-stdin execution only. Autonomous kickoff, structured decomposition, provider policy dials, and containers fail with an explicit capability error for custom. Legacy binary-only configurations still infer Claude, Codex, or custom semantics; repositories with neither field continue to default to Claude.
Provider model settings use semantic tiers so orchestration does not leak one provider’s model names into another provider’s command line:
{
  "agent": {
    "providers": {
      "claude": {
        "standard_model": "sonnet",
        "advanced_model": "opus"
      },
      "codex": {
        "standard_model": null,
        "advanced_model": null,
        "sandbox": "workspace-write",
        "approval": "auto-review"
      }
    }
  }
}
A null Codex model leaves the signed-in account’s current default in control. Automatic review keeps the host sandbox enabled while allowing Codex to request the narrowly elevated Git metadata writes needed for kickoff commits; Codex protects .git from ordinary workspace-write commands. Kickoff, plan, swarm, sentinel, design, orchestrator decomposition, containers, and dashboard monitoring all use the same resolver and invocation adapter.

Related issues







Command
Description




crosslink issue relate &lt;id1&gt; &lt;id2&gt;
Link two related issues


crosslink issue unrelate &lt;id1&gt; &lt;id2&gt;
Remove relationship


crosslink issue related &lt;id&gt;
List issues related to the given issue

Milestones







Command
Description




crosslink milestone create &lt;name&gt;
Create a milestone


crosslink milestone create &lt;name&gt; -d "desc"
Create with description


crosslink milestone list
List all milestones


crosslink milestone show &lt;id&gt;
Show milestone details and progress


crosslink milestone add &lt;milestone_id&gt; &lt;issue_id&gt;
Add issue to milestone


crosslink milestone remove &lt;milestone_id&gt; &lt;issue_id&gt;
Remove issue from milestone


crosslink milestone close &lt;id&gt;
Close a milestone


crosslink milestone delete &lt;id&gt;
Delete a milestone

